---
title: How to Add and Manage Tax in Taskip for Invoices and Quotations
sidebar:
  order: 17
---
**Taskip allows you to create and manage tax classes that can be applied to both invoices and quotations. Whether you’re charging VAT, GST, or a custom tax, you can configure multiple tax entries, search them dynamically, and even create new taxes directly while creating a document.**

### **How to Add a New Tax Class**

*How to Add a New Tax Class*

**1. Go to Settings\
From the sidebar, click on Settings.**

**2. Navigate to Tax Settings\
Under the Settings menu, select Tax Settings.**

**3. Click “Add New Tax”\
On the top-right corner, click the Add New Tax button to open the tax creation form.**

***Add New Tax***

**4. Fill Out Tax Details**

- **Tax Name: Provide a clear name such as `VAT` or `Service Tax`.**
- **Tax Rate (%): Enter the percentage rate, e.g., `10` for 10%.**

**Click Add Tax to save.**

**Once added, the tax class will be available globally and can be reused across invoices and quotations.**

### **Applying Tax in Invoices and Quotations**

*Applying Tax in Invoices and Quotations*

**1. Create or Edit an Invoice or Quotation\
Open an existing invoice/quotation or start a new one.**

**2. Scroll to the Total Section\
Locate the Add Tax field in the totals area below your listed items.**

**3. Search or Select a Tax Class\
Click on the Add Tax dropdown to:**

- **Search existing tax classes**
- **Select one or multiple taxes to apply**

**4. Add New Tax from the Dropdown\
If you need a new tax:**

- **Click the dropdown**
- **Choose the option to Add New Tax**
- **Fill out the Tax Name and Tax Rate (%)**
- **Save, and it will be instantly available for use**

### **Key Features**

- **Supports multiple tax classes for different regions or tax types**
- **Tax rates are calculated automatically and reflected in the Total**
- **Applies uniformly to both invoices and quotations**
- **Allows inline tax creation for speed and flexibility**
- **Automatically updates available tax options across the workspace**

### **Best Practices**

- **Name taxes clearly (e.g., `GST 18%`) for quick recognition**
- **Review tax policies applicable to your region before adding new entries**
- **Use consistent naming and rates to avoid confusion across documents**
- **Apply taxes at the time of quotation for accurate client estimates**

### **Frequently Asked Questions (FAQ)**

### **Can I add more than one tax to a single invoice or quotation?**

**Yes. You can apply multiple tax classes to the same document.**

### **Will the applied tax be calculated automatically?**

**Yes. Taskip automatically calculates the tax amount and adds it to the total.**

### **Can I add a new tax while editing a document? [\#](https://taskip.net/docs/add-manage-tax-taskip-invoice-quotation/#7-toc-title)**

**Yes. You can create a new tax directly from the tax dropdown while editing an invoice or quotation.**

### **Can I apply different tax rates to different items?**

**Currently, taxes are applied at the document level. Item-level tax support may be added in future versions.**

### **Is the tax applied the same for both invoices and quotations?**

**Yes. The tax system is shared and consistent across both modules.**
